                "linkedin": "# Building Boundaries While Raising a Toddler: The Chaos I Never Planned For\n\nTwo years ago, my husband and I sat at our kitchen table with spreadsheets, wireframes, and a half-eaten box of cereal. We were building something we called \"Guardd\"-a platform designed to help families navigate the messy intersection of kids and technology. At the time, our biggest child-related concern was whether our then-baby could roll off the changing pad.\n\nFast forward two years and twenty pounds lighter per parent (the baby weighs more now), and here I am-building the very product we need most for ourselves.\n\n## What Nobody Tells You About Toddlers and Screens\n\nWhen you're pregnant, people hand you pamphlets about car seat safety, infant CPR, and breastfeeding positions. Nobody hands you a guide on managing screen-time meltdowns at the grocery store checkout lane. My daughter discovered how to unlock my iPad at eighteen months old using what can only be described as criminal intent. She didn't accidentally tap the screen-she swiped through three apps before finding TikTok.\n\n(She watched four seconds of someone making pancakes before I intervened.)\n\nThe point isn't that she's prodigious. It's that toddlers figure out screens faster than parents figure out boundaries. And by the time you've established one rule, your child has already found a loophole involving your smart speaker.\n\n## The Rule That Almost Broke Us\n\nOur first boundary attempt went spectacularly wrong within forty-eight hours. We set up a simple timer app (\"ten minutes of cartoons, then screen goes dark!\") and announced it like a presidential executive order.\n\nShe screamed for eleven minutes straight.\n\nNot regular screaming-I mean full-body, tectonic-event, neighbors-comment-on-it screaming. Our dog hid under the couch.\n\n#DigitalGuardian #DigitalParenting #DigitalSafety #ParentingTips",
                "bluesky": "# Building Boundaries While Raising a Toddler: The Chaos I Never Planned For\n\nTwo years ago, my husband and I sat at our kitchen table with spreadsheets, wireframes, and a half-eaten box of cereal.\n\nWant to read more?... check out my LinkedIn"
