            "carousel": [],
            "captions": {
                "linkedin": "No-Phone Zones: Where They Work (and Why)\n\nHey everyone - quick poll before I share our experience.\n\nDoes your family have a no-phones-at-the-table rule? If yes, how do you handle it?\n\n\ud83c\udfe0 At home\n\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f Dinnertime\n\ud83d\udec1 Bedtime routines\n\u26be Family outings/activities\nAll of these\nNone yet!\n\nFor us, dinner was always non-negotiable from day one. Even at two years old, my daughter knows phones stay on the counter during meals. She'll point at them if she sees mine sitting next to her plate. \ud83d\ude05 It's become this little unspoken agreement.\n\nBut here's what surprised me - the dining table rule alone doesn't carry over everywhere else automatically. We learned that the hard way after an afternoon at the park where we were all buried in screens instead of actually being there. Now we try to extend those same boundaries to car rides, waiting rooms, even just hanging out on weekends.\n\nThe research backs up why this matters. A study from the [University of Michigan](https://news.umich.edu/the-dinner-conversation-has-a-bigger-impact-on-kids-than-you-might-expect/) found that meaningful conversation during family dinners predicted better social development later on. And according to Common Sense Media, kids notice their parents' screen habits more than almost anything else we model.\n\nSo whether your boundary is dinner, bedtime, or weekend mornings - what matters isn't which zone you pick. It's that you pick one and stick with it consistently enough that it becomes part of your family's rhythm rather than something you police constantly.\n\nVote above, then drop your best tip for making it work in the comments. I'm collecting honest answers for an upcoming guide on manageable household tech agreements.\n\nAnd if you're still figuring yours out - start small. One meal, one room, one hour.\n\n#DigitalGuardian #DigitalParenting #DigitalSafety #ParentingTips",
                "bluesky": "No-Phone Zones: Where They Work (and Why)\n\nHey everyone - quick poll before I share our experience.\n\nDoes your family have a no-phones-at-the-table rule? If yes, how do you handle it?\n\n\ud83c\udfe0 At home\n\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f Dinnertime\n\ud83d\udec1 Bedtime routines\n\nWant to read more?... check out my LinkedIn"
